.* OPTICAL: the task menu for optical support.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='OPTICAL'.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKDEVD PNLGRP=QHCFCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKMLBSTS PNLGRP=QHSVCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKOPTVOL PNLGRP=QHOPCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=OPTICAL HELP=HLPOPTICAL KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Optical Support Utilities
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKOPTVOL' HELP=WRKOPTVOL.Work with optical volumes
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ?WRKOPTDIR' HELP='OPTICAL/OPT2'.Work with optical directories
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?WRKOPTF' HELP='OPTICAL/OPT3'.Work with optical files
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD WRKMLBSTS' HELP=WRKMLBSTS.Work with optical libraries
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD WRKDEVD DEVD(*OPT)' HELP=WRKDEVD.Work with optical devices
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='MENU RECOVERY' HELP='OPTICAL/OPT6'.Optical backup/recovery menu
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='MENU OPTSERVER' HELP='OPTICAL/OPT7'.Optical server menu
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPOPTICAL.Optical Support Utilities - Help
:P.The optical volumes, libraries and devices of this system, virtual or
real.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPTICAL/OPT2'.Work with optical directories
:P.Option 2. Runs the WRKOPTDIR command&colon. Work with optical
directories.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPTICAL/OPT3'.Work with optical files
:P.Option 3. Runs the WRKOPTF command&colon. Work with optical files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPTICAL/OPT6'.Optical backup/recovery menu
:P.Option 6. Shows menu RECOVERY&colon. Optical backup/recovery menu.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OPTICAL/OPT7'.Optical server menu
:P.Option 7. Shows menu OPTSERVER&colon. Optical server menu.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
